# Generated benchmark matrices. datasets/generate_matrices.py rebuilds every one
# of these (seeded, so byte-identical on any machine), which makes committing them
# pure repository weight - and matrixA_3072.txt at 225 MB is over GitHub's hard
# 100 MB per-file push limit. Regenerate with:
#     python datasets/generate_matrices.py
#
# Written as two literal patterns rather than one matrix[AB]_*.txt class: git
# sets core.ignorecase=true on a case-insensitive filesystem (the macOS
# default), and under casefolding it lowercases the candidate path but not the
# characters inside a bracket expression, so [AB] stops matching a capital A.
# The class form silently fails to ignore anything on exactly the machines this
# project is developed on.
matrixA_*.txt
matrixB_*.txt
datasets/matrixA_*.txt
datasets/matrixB_*.txt

# Git internals that were committed by accident
FETCH_HEAD

# Editor backup files
*.save
*~
*.bak

# CMake / build output
build/
compile_commands.json
# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
